0001-mps-device-aware-energy-accumulation.patch    APPLIED on studio-2 (~/venvs/imcc-md)

What it fixes: mace/modules/models.py:581 hard-casts node_energy accumulation to
float64 (.double()); Apple MPS has no float64, so every forward pass on MPS crashes
even with float32 checkpoints. The patch makes the accumulation dtype device-aware:
float64 wherever the device supports it (behaviour unchanged on CPU/CUDA), the model
working dtype on MPS.

